```c
for (p = name; *p && *p != '.'; p++)
{
    if (*p == '\\' && *(p + 1) != 0)
        p++;
    len++;
}
```

This counts the actual characters (skipping backslashes). But the label length byte takes one byte, and then:
```c
*q++ = (unsigned char)len;
for (p = name; *p && *p != '.'; p++)
{
    if (*p == '\\' && *(p + 1) != 0)
        p++;
    *q++ = *p;
